+    - type: Paper
+      content: >-
+        This is the Thermo-Electric Generator (TEG) and is the only main generator to Atlas besides the AME. the TEG is a very powerful generator that can produce power in the Megawatts if setup correctly, which should be enough for the station and more. The following is a guide for how to setup the generator.
+
+
+        (1). General Overview
+
+        The TEG produces power via a temperature difference in both of it's circulators. Specific heat capacity, flow rate, and the amount of gasses in both circulators can also effect the TEG's output.
+
+
+        (1.1) Specific Heat Capacity and More
+
+        Specific heat capcity is a property of all substances and is how thermal energy effects the substance, for example a substance with a high specific heat capacity can absorb a lot of energy without increasing their temperature too much, while a substance with a low specific can absorb little energy to increase their temperature a lot.
+
+        Now how is this useful for the TEG? Well, a high energy difference is needed, so it might seem at first that a gas with a low specific heat capacity would be best because it'd heat up the most, but it isn't! due to the high increase in temperature, pressure will quickly rise, and assuming pressure is being regulated to be below 9000kPa, the circulators pressure limit, less moles will then be in the loop. So a gas with a high specific heat capcity will be best being able to absorb more thermal energy. Two plasma canister are normaly provided for this effort, being a gas with a high specific heat capcity.
+
+
+        (2) The Hot and Cold Loops
+
+        As somewhat hinted before, for both the TEG's circulators, to recieve hot and cold gasses, two loops will be needed for both temperature extremes.
+
+
+        (2.1) The Cold Loop
+
+        For the TEG's temperature difference to be reached and power produced, one circulator will need to be colder than the other. But how can this be achieved? Radiators is the answer, they will release the thermal energy of gasses within itself assuming their environment is colder than the radiator's contents. For this to be the most effective, radiators in the cold loop can be placed in space on lattice. Keep in mind that radiators work off a pressure difference, therefore increasing the flow rate between radiators will increase their energy released.
+
+        Thermo-machines, such as freezers and their hellfire varients, may be used as well to cool down the loop as well.
+
+
+        (2.2) The Hot Loop
+
+        As stated before for the TEG to be complete one of it's loops must be hotter or colder than the other, so how can we heat up a loop? A contained plasma fire is normaly used. A line filled with a burn mix of around 97% oxygen and 3% plasma should be injected into the provided chamber. Place some radiators inside the chamber for the hot loop to absorb the released energy within the reaction. Once the chamber is full light it, and the loop should begin to heat up. Make sure to have some system to either cool down or release gasses within the chamber to keep it running.
+         Unlike the cold loop thermo-machines, such as heaters and their hellfire varients, should not be used as the hot loop will normally reach upwards of 5000K which no heater can achieve.
+
+        (3) Pressure regulation
+
+        As stated beforehand in (1.1) pressure regulation is needed within the hot loop and possibly the cold loop if too much gas is injected. Circulators will stop functioning past a pressure of 9000kPa and will halt the TEG's power production. Due to the nature of the hot loop heating up it's pressure will rise forewhich an inlet pressure regulator can be used to release some of the loops gas if pressure goes above 9000kPa (or whatever pressure you'd like to set the regulator to). As a note, it's most ideal to situate the regulator before the circulators input. If not, when over pressure occurs the over pressured gas won't reach the pressure regulator due to the circulator halting.
+
+
+        (4) Final Notes
+
+        That should be all you need to setup the TEG, I know that was a lot but this machine isnt exactly simple in full detail, which is why a TL;DR was writen below here. Also this guide doesn't need to be followed, loops don't need to be used at all, only a temperature difference is needed and you are free to use whatever design you'd like.
+
+
+
+        TL;DR
+
+        TEG for dummies
+
+
+        (1) Warning
+
+        Keep in mind this should only be used in emergancy or if stuck on the regualar guide above, if you are reading this and those two points dont apply to you then I urge to fully understand this generator rather than just get it running.
+
+
+        (2) Main guide
+
+        Two loops are needed, hot and cold, both with plasma.
+
+
+        (2.1) Cold Loop
+
+        Mostly setup already, just connect the line to the northern most circulator with pumps directly at the input and output of the circulator to maximis flow rate, then inject plasma into the loop with a connector port with a plasma canister anchored to it.
+
+
+        (2.2) Hot Loop
+
+        Exact same as the cold loop but requires a inlet pressure regulator at the pipe before the pump connected to the loop's circulator input. At the output for the inlet pressure regulator, space a tile in the TEG room and place a passive vent on that spaced tile to release the plasma.
+
+
+        (2.2.1) Burn Chamber
+
+        Hook up the brown line in atmos with a burn mix of 97% oxygen and 3% plasma and pump that into the burn chamber. Lit the chamber with a welder and then keep the door open so the chamber can keep running.
+
+
+        (3) Final Notes
+
+        With that the TEG should be active and power flowing to Atlas' SMES banks.
+
+
+        Best of luck,
+
+
+        Michael
